==Regional Soja Shrines== Regional Soja Shrines are Soja shrines dedicated to a specific region rather than a whole province. These include
* {{ill|Akasaka Uenoyama Shrine|ja|赤坂上之山神社}} * {{ill|Unakoro Waki Shrine|ja|宇奈己呂和気神社}} * {{ill|Ono Shrine (Ritto City)|ja|大野神社 (栗東市)}} * {{ill|Ogami Shrine (Tonami City)|ja|雄神神社 (砺波市)}} * {{ill|Kainan Shrine|ja|海南神社}} * {{ill|Katsushika Shrine|ja|葛飾神社}} * {{ill|Katsube Shrine|ja|勝部神社}} * {{ill|Mukuhashi Shrine|ja|椋橋総社}} * {{ill|Kotai Jingu (Fujisawa City)|ja|皇大神宮 (藤沢市)}} * {{ill|Gosho Shrine (Sammu City)|ja|五所神社 (山武市)}} * {{ill|Sakata Shinmei Shrine|ja|坂田神明宮}} * {{ill|Shinkai Sansha Shrine|ja|新海三社神社}} * {{ill|Sazama Shrine (Daito City)|ja|坐摩神社 (大東市)}} * {{ill|Kenda Suga Shrine|ja|健田須賀神社}} * {{ill|Tachibana Shrine (Kawasaki City)|ja|橘樹神社 (川崎市)}} * {{ill|Torakashi Shrine|ja|虎柏神社}} * [[Nagao Shrine]] * {{ill|Nanba Shrine|ja|難波神社|de|Namba-Schrein|fr|Namba-jinja|simple}} (may have historically been a provincial one) * {{ill|Arayaza Amaterasu Mitama Shrine|ja|新屋坐天照御魂神社}} * {{ill|Nogi Shrine (Tokyo)|lt=Nogi Shrine|ja|能義神社}} * {{ill|Hotaka Shrine|ja|穂高神社|simple}} * [[Washinomiya Shrine]]
